  "description": "CR 717.2b a Class retains its level even if it stops being a Class",
  "note": "Song of the Dryads makes the Class a colourless Forest land: Land replaces Enchantment, and the Class subtype goes with the type it correlates with (CR 205.1a, 205.3h). The retention shows across the round trip: the same Aura strips the abilities (CR 305.7), so the level-2 section is off while it is on whatever the level says. The Class is levelled to 2 first, so a level lost while it was not a Class would leave it at CR 717.2d's 1 and the Piker 2/1 once Aura Graft moves the Song onto the Mountain. The Haskell test moves the Aura directly and reads the level; here Aura Graft moves it, and the level is read through the bars: the level-2 bar refused and the level-3 bar taken.",
